{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "title": "Title",
      "text": "%md\n# My CTRP notebook: exploring the data and building the features\n\nSame steps and same numbers as the review note \"CTRP EDA and features\", written step by step.\n\nFeature names say what is measured, per what, over which window, and end with the unit, for example\n`topped_up_per_decl_3y_rate`. Short forms: decl, peer (other importers' middle price), hs4, coo, exempt, pref, dev,\navg, qtr. Track B columns start with `b_`, percentiles end with `pct`, Track A values before the small-numbers step\nstart with `raw_`.\n\n1. Settings and setup\n2. Load the data from the view\n3. Explore it: size, missing data, duplicates, values\n4. The 13 data problems, one by one, with evidence\n5. Clean the data\n6. Declarations\n7. Track A features (8)\n8. Track B features (17)\n9. Recency, small numbers, peer groups\n10. The final dataset",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_mine_000",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_mine_000",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "text": "%pyspark\n# ---------- settings (the only cell to change) ----------\nSNAPSHOT = '2026-09-30'          # the date the risk profile is made\nWITH_OUTCOMES = False              # True for a past date: also count what happened in the 6 months after\nSAMPLE_1_IN = None                 # 20 = try it on 1 in 20 taxpayers first. None = everyone\n\nEXCLUDE_APC_483 = True              # rule R13\nLATEST_DECLARATION_PER_ENTRY = True    # rule R14\nEXCLUDE_MOTOR_VEHICLES = True          # rule R15\nMOTOR_VEHICLE_HEADINGS = ['8701', '8702', '8703', '8704', '8705', '8706', '8707', '8708', '8711']\n\nSAVE_TO_FOLDER = False             # True = also write CSV files to OUT_DIR\nOUT_DIR = '/user/CHANGE_ME/ctrp_eda_mine'\nSAVE_TO_SCHEMA = None              # a Hive schema I can write to, if I get one\n\nVIEW = 'dm_modeled_ura_datascience.vw_cstm_AEO_model'",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_mine_001",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_mine_001",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "Setup",
      "text": "%pyspark\nimport datetime\nimport calendar\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport pyspark.sql.functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef month_end(date_text, months):\n    # last day of the month that is `months` away from the date (negative = before)\n    d = datetime.datetime.strptime(date_text, '%Y-%m-%d').date()\n    total_months = d.year * 12 + d.month - 1 + months\n    year = total_months // 12\n    month = total_months % 12 + 1\n    last_day = calendar.monthrange(year, month)[1]\n    return datetime.date(year, month, last_day)\n\n\n# the view stores dates as text like '20260930', so I keep my dates in the same format\nSNAP = datetime.datetime.strptime(SNAPSHOT, '%Y-%m-%d').strftime('%Y%m%d')\nHIST_START = month_end(SNAPSHOT, -24).strftime('%Y%m%d')     # features: 24 months\nHIST3_START = month_end(SNAPSHOT, -36).strftime('%Y%m%d')    # recency: 36 months\nPRIOR_START = month_end(SNAPSHOT, -60).strftime('%Y%m%d')    # new trader check: the 3 years before that\nif WITH_OUTCOMES:\n    OUT_END = month_end(SNAPSHOT, 6).strftime('%Y%m%d')\nelse:\n    OUT_END = SNAP\nsnap_date = F.to_date(F.lit(SNAPSHOT))\n\n\ndef save_table(df, name):\n    # keep a result as a table in this session (and write it out if switched on)\n    if isinstance(df, pd.DataFrame):\n        df = spark.createDataFrame(df)\n    df.createOrReplaceTempView(name)\n    if SAVE_TO_FOLDER:\n        df.coalesce(1).write.mode('overwrite').option('header', True).csv(OUT_DIR + '/' + name)\n    if SAVE_TO_SCHEMA:\n        df.write.mode('overwrite').saveAsTable(SAVE_TO_SCHEMA + '.' + name)\n\n\nprint('snapshot', SNAP, '| features from', HIST_START, '| recency from', HIST3_START, '| data up to', OUT_END)",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
